1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
[A1] Elder fraud now costs families over ten billion dollars a year. Threats. Fake arrests. Stolen passwords. In Vadodara, one family decided to fight back.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:24,550
[D1] Beta, a bank message came. They want my OTP. What do I do?

3
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:34,390
[K1] Ruko, Dadaji. Do nothing. Look, the phone never even buzzed. Kavach locked the scam away before you could touch it.

4
00:00:34,390 --> 00:00:50,090
[K2] See? Every reason cited. Asked for OTP. Threatened arrest. Fake urgency. I blocked the number from my office. When they called back, the phone killed it before the first ring.

5
00:00:50,090 --> 00:01:04,060
[K3] And it learns. Signed rules, fresh this morning, verified on the phone itself. One family's block now protects every family. Hashes only. Never phone numbers.

6
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:13,420
[K4] The server? It holds nothing but noise. Ciphertext and hashes. There is nothing here worth stealing.

7
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:26,910
[A2] Protection for dadaji. Peace for papa. Kavach, built by thirteen year old Krishiv Joshi of Vadodara. Open source. MIT licensed.
